# Refactor Gate

Runs during `/refactor` after implementation. Do not mark a feature complete until all checks pass.

## When to run

After `/implement` completes and before `/architect`.

## Scripts

From repository root:

```powershell
./scripts/run-cyclomatic-complexity.ps1 -Threshold 6
./scripts/run-roslyn-analyzers.ps1
./scripts/run-jetbrains-inspectcode.ps1
./scripts/run-property-tests.ps1
dotnet test
```

## Threshold

Methods on changed files MUST be at or under `gates.complexity.refactor` in `harness.yml` (default **6**) — deliberately stricter than the implementation ceiling `gates.complexity.implement` (default 15).

Two thresholds, not one, because the bar tightens once the code works: 15 is what you are allowed to write while solving the problem, 6 is what you are allowed to keep.

## Property tests

Add FsCheck property tests for pure/domain logic in changed code. Tag with `[Trait("Category", "Property")]`.

## Failure handling

- CA1502 violations: extract helpers, early returns — no suppressions unless generated code
- DuplicatedCode (InspectCode): refactor before proceeding
- Property test failures: fix implementation or shrink generator inputs
